  "details": "VRChat Version: Build 1220, however it happened in previous versions too.\n\n\nDescription of the bug:\nI have my controller bindings in the VRChat settings set to SteamVR. If I change the binding for the Mic Toggle to be on something else and then press that button it will detect my thumb being down on my left hand, even when it isn't.\nIn my case I have it on right trackpad on the Index Controllers but I've tested it on other buttons and the same issue occurs.\nThis is consistantly reproducible and happens no matter the avatar.\nI don't know when this started to happen or if it's always been an issue but I've only recently noticed it since I've been testing the personal mirror a bit and I see my gestures mess up when I toggle mute.\n\n\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\nSet your VRChat controller bindings to use SteamVR in the ingame VRChat settings.\nChange your binding so that Mic Toggle is on another button (in my case right it's Index Controller trackpad. Use as button, click)\nToggle gestures on ingame and either open debug menu or turn on gesture indicator.\nDo finger gun on the left hand and press the newly assigned mic toggle. It will change to finger point. You'll also see your thumb go from the neutral/up position to the down position.",
